From db61dc6029d1c2636608c101c3fb72fa73549de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 20:06:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05811/11362] [outer-loop] fix the human replay corpus staging
 bug: regenerate the full corpus

Operator authorized starting ARC-specific work directly in the outer loop
given available quota headroom. This is the first task picked up, per
yesterday's research note diagnosing the staging bug.

Root cause confirmed precisely: exp4495's own recorded
training_shard_count=3/training_example_count=10000 shows the original
2026-06-20 run only ever staged the "10k truncated mirror" per the
manifest's own note. A later, undocumented partial restaging reached 4
shards / 14,797 examples on disk -- still far short of the full
340-session raw corpus -- and every row's level_progress read
degenerately 0.0.

Verified the conversion code itself
(python/carnot/agentic/arc_human_replay_corpus.py) is correct, not
buggy: tested it directly against the raw parquet mirror and confirmed
level_progress transitions from 0.0 to 0.125 exactly at the right
action-index boundary (level 1 completing at step 37 of a real winning
session). The bug was purely that the on-disk staged output was
stale/incomplete, never regenerated with the full raw corpus after
whatever produced the truncated version. No code changes were needed.

Re-ran write_training_shards_from_parquet() against all 7 already-
downloaded raw parquet files (626.5s). Result: 180,144 examples across
44 shards (was 14,797/4), spanning 339 distinct sessions across all 25
public games. Validated directly by scanning all 44 regenerated shards:
93.2% of rows now carry non-zero level_progress (was 0%), 17.0% show
level_progress=1.0 (fully won) -- matching the raw source's own
144-winning-session ground truth from yesterday's investigation.

results/experiment_4495_human_replay_corpus_staging.json updated with
the corrected shard state (training_shard_count, training_example_count,
shard_checksums) and a full corrigendum documenting the incident.
adversarial_verify.py clean (0 flags). The artifact's own test suite (10
tests) still passes after patching.

This unblocks exp4490 (the original frame-change-predictor task, blocked
since 2026-06-20 04:40, never retried in the two weeks since) and the
TRM-as-generator leave-one-game-out pilot -- the training-data-
sufficiency question is no longer just resolved-in-principle, the
corpus is genuinely usable on disk now.

data/arc_public_demo_human_replay_corpus/ is gitignored (large binary
corpus); the regenerated shards/manifest live there but are not part of
this commit -- only the result artifact + research notes are tracked.

